    "limitations": [
        "SSE body bytes only; excludes HTTP/TCP/TLS and follow-up HTTP reads. Not a latency or capacity benchmark.",
        "Before/after encoders receive identical payloads and emission timestamps; the reference retains the old redundant timer.server_time field.",
        "All 12 registry commands are covered, including the read-only reserve command; this is not exhaustive coverage of every argument/lineup/score permutation.",
        "Editor/lineup/provider writes and asynchronous statistics job publications are not individually profiled.",
        "Control frames use the included synthetic UUID and revision 123. Ready is an already-current compact reconnect with no live clock payload. Legacy match and tournament samples are invalidation-only; their downstream GET cost is excluded.",
        "Duplicate-bootstrap savings apply when a snapshot was already queued for that joining connection; they are not an unconditional 50% startup reduction.",
        "Compact metadata, dictionaries, snapshots, legacy compatibility and tournament invalidation payloads retain their existing formats."
